    "doi": "https://doi.org/10.26599/ifungi.2026.9670003",
    "abstract": "Pathogenic fungal infections represent an escalating public health priority in China. This review synthesizes the evolving threat landscape, characterized by the concurrent challenges of emerging pathogens and rising antifungal resistance across clinical and environmental settings. It examines the expanding high-risk demographics\u2014specifically immunocompromised hosts and those with healthcare-associated exposures\u2014while analyzing the synergistic roles of climate change and human activities in accelerating transmission dynamics. By consolidating current epidemiological data on representative fungi, this article highlights critical gaps in current disease management. We propose a strategic framework centered on strengthening integrated monitoring systems, implementing robust antimicrobial stewardship, and adopting a proactive, preventative paradigm for vulnerable populations. Crucially, the review advocates for a comprehensive \u201cOne Health\u201d approach to mitigate the environmental and ecological drivers of fungal spread. These perspectives provide a strategic roadmap for policymakers and clinicians to fortify a resilient defense against the growing burden of fungal diseases in China.",
    "field": "Public health risks of pathogenic fungi",
    "problem": "The public health risk from pathogenic fungi in China is escalating due to a convergence of challenges, including emerging pathogens, rising antifungal resistance, expanding vulnerable populations, and environmental changes that accelerate transmission dynamics and strain current disease management systems.",
    "method": "The paper proposes a strategic framework centered on a \"One Health\" approach that integrates strengthened surveillance, robust antimicrobial stewardship, and proactive prevention to mitigate the growing public health risks of pathogenic fungi in China.",
    "task": "The task is to review the escalating public health risks of pathogenic fungi in China and propose a comprehensive strategic framework, using a \"One Health\" approach, to mitigate these threats.",
